My only problem with this is that it create further complexity to the logic, if you wish to enable time travelling queries based on a condition.

E.g. it's not possible to do:

```ts
queryBuilder.timeTravelQuery(false) // disable all TTQ
queryBuilder.timeTravelQuery(shouldUseTTQ) // disable all TTQ based on condition
```

Instead you need to do something like:

```ts
const query = this.userRepository
.createQueryBuilder('user')
.where({...})
.select(['user.id']);

if(shouldTimeTravel) {
	query.timeTravelQuery();
}

return query.getRawMany();

